# Pinned commit of github.com/mstan/snesrecomp used to build this repo.
# Bumping this is a deliberate, reviewable change (snesrecomp is a separate
# repo evolving on its own cadence). Update via:
#   git -C ./snesrecomp rev-parse dev/super-metroid > /tmp/sha && \
#     sed -i "s|^sha = .*|sha = $(cat /tmp/sha)|" snesrecomp.pin
sha = 279d7877a0e9d23b9df2fbf7c3e9b04a4842a161
# 2026-07-14 DerrickGold candidate integration validated in Super Metroid at
# authentic 4:3: SimpleHDMA bounds, bank sharding, opt-in widescreen policies,
# no-sprite-limits support, and the filtered interpreter policy hook.
# 2026-07-14 interpreter non-local return checkpoint: direct AOT bounces
# preserve guest returns that unwind through an interpreted caller.
# 2026-07-13 HLE/LLE boundary checkpoint (e0520dd -> 88c41ad): HLE
# overlays cover every exact runtime M/X mode and consume inherited tail-call
# metadata, while architectural LLE remains the fallback for non-overlaid code.
# 2026-07-13 LLE-first redesign checkpoint: deterministic whole-program
# analysis, atomic cached emission, RTI-aware mixed AOT/LLE interrupt tails,
# and profile promotion restricted to proven function boundaries.
# 2026-07-13 fold checkpoint (19cb7cb -> aeab6c0): records the engine used by
# the validated LLE gameplay build: interruptible ROM waits, mixed-tier return
# continuations, stack/return-PC guards, immediate hardware-visible APU ports,
# and link-safe partial regeneration. The old pin described the initial
# bring-up generator but no longer matched the live engine junction used by
# the committed Ceres, door, pause, and ship-save fixes.
# Branch: main. Super Metroid bring-up is folding onto the shared engine main.
#
# 19cb7cb (2026-06-11): dev/super-metroid tip — the framework the current
# recomp/*.cfg actually require. The prior pin (d8566c4, 2026-06-08) was
# STALE: the cfgs use the `indirect_dispatch ... ptrcall` directive form
# (the 2026-06-09 cinematic-dispatch work), which d8566c4's cfg_loader does
# NOT understand — v2_sync_funcs_h.py fails there with "indirect_dispatch
# unknown option 'ptrcall'", and a regen at d8566c4 silently leaves those
# dispatches unresolved. Verified 2026-06-12: regen + funcs.h sync + build
# all succeed against 19cb7cb (the matched pair to this repo's Codex
# checkpoint c231950).
#
# d8566c4 (2026-06-08) had: variant-prune protected-set, $4212 synthetic
# vblank counter, inline-argument decoder, boot-spin watchdog. 19cb7cb adds
# the ptrcall dispatch form + the rest of the ~15h bring-up session.
